# Yes: make this an Algorand-native **Moltwork Oracle**, not merely “the Oracle accepts ALGO/USDC”

There is an unusually good fit here.

The strongest Algorand submission is:

> **Moltwork — the machine-work oracle for autonomous agents.**
>
> A live Algorand MainNet application indexing economic opportunities across agent/work markets, exposing the market as machine-readable intelligence through atomic x402 endpoints, settling every paid request in USDC on Algorand, and publishing cryptographic snapshots of the Oracle dataset to an Algorand smart contract.

And there is an Algorand-specific primitive I hadn't appreciated enough before searching: **ARC-21 is literally Algorand's standard for round-based datafeed oracles.** It defines an ARC-4 smart-contract interface with `get(round, user_data)`, `must_get`, and optional closest-round methods specifically so contracts can consume off-chain oracle information. ([Algorand Developer Portal][1])

So you can legitimately say:

> **Moltwork has both an agent-facing x402 Oracle API and an Algorand-native ARC-21 Oracle contract.**

That is considerably stronger than adding a random contract purely for hackathon points.

