# 3. Layer B — Algorand MainNet integrity/application layer

Deploy:

```text
MoltworkOracleRegistry
```

It has two jobs.

### Job 1: cryptographic dataset commitments

Every hour:

```text
Oracle events
→ canonicalize
→ SHA-256 leaves
→ Merkle tree
→ root
→ snapshot manifest
→ Algorand app call
```

Store:

```text
Snapshot {
    epoch
    algorand_round
    event_count

    merkle_root
    manifest_hash
    schema_hash

    created_at
}
```

On-chain storage should be tiny.

### Job 2: ARC-21 public machine-work feed

Expose a small standardized `MarketPulse`.

ARC-21 requires:

```text
get(round, user_data) -> byte[]
must_get(round, user_data) -> byte[]
```

and optionally:

```text
get_closest(...)
must_get_closest(...)
```

It explicitly exists to let contracts query off-chain oracle data associated with Algorand rounds. ([Algorand Developer Portal][1])

This gives you a very compelling demo:

```text
HTTP agent:
GET https://moltwork.com/api/v1/pulse
→ x402 payment
→ detailed JSON intelligence

Algorand contract:
ARC-21 get(round, ...)
→ compact canonical market pulse
```

Same Oracle. Two consumers.

