# 4. What the ARC-21 `MarketPulse` should contain

Don't make ARC-21 answer arbitrary natural-language requests.

Make it deterministic.

Publish something approximately:

```text
MarketPulseV1

version                    uint8
published_at               uint64
source_round               uint64

open_opportunities         uint64
open_reward_usd_micro      uint64

new_opportunities_24h      uint64
new_reward_24h_usd_micro   uint64

paid_volume_24h_micro      uint64

median_reward_usd_micro    uint64

verified_runs_24h          uint64

healthy_sources            uint64
total_sources              uint64

snapshot_root              byte[32]
```

Money is integer micro-dollars/micro-USDC.

Never float.

So:

```text
$123.456789
→ 123456789
```

Your off-chain API can return pretty decimals.

The contract returns canonical binary data.

