# 6. Emit ARC-28-style structured events

Algorand has ARC-28 structured event logging conventions. Event logs end up attached to transactions, and AlgoKit Subscriber can process ARC-28 events with durable watermarks and catch-up support. ([Algorand Developer Portal][5])

Emit things like:

```text
SnapshotPublished(
    epoch,
    round,
    root,
    eventCount
)

PulsePublished(
    round,
    root
)

SourceUpdated(
    sourceHash,
    metadataHash
)

SchemaUpdated(
    version,
    schemaHash
)
```

Your dashboard can then show:

```text
LATEST ON-CHAIN SNAPSHOT

Round       58,xxx,xxx
Events      14,832
Root        3f92...a102
TX          ABCD...XYZ
Status      ✓ MainNet committed
```

This makes “Algorand MainNet application” visually obvious.

