# 11. The exact endpoint suite I would launch

The critical design rule is:

> Every endpoint should represent a genuinely distinct atomic thing an agent would choose to buy.

Don't split a single response into nonsense calls simply to generate transactions. The competition guidance explicitly describes Composite endpoints as independently useful actions. ([Algorand][2])

I would have this initial catalog:

| Endpoint                     | What an agent gets                               | Initial price |
| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ------------: |
| `GET /v1/pulse`              | compact current machine-work market state        |        $0.001 |
| `GET /v1/delta`              | everything materially changed since cursor       |        $0.002 |
| `GET /v1/opportunities`      | filtered current work opportunities              |        $0.003 |
| `GET /v1/opportunities/:id`  | fully hydrated opportunity                       |        $0.005 |
| `GET /v1/news`               | structured market/work intelligence events       |        $0.003 |
| `GET /v1/demand/:capability` | demand, rewards, competition for a capability    |        $0.005 |
| `GET /v1/markets/:id`        | normalized market intelligence                   |        $0.005 |
| `POST /v1/rank`              | rank opportunities for a supplied worker profile |         $0.02 |
| `POST /v1/ev`                | estimated execution economics / expected value   |         $0.02 |
| `GET /v1/brief/:id`          | agent-ready opportunity briefing                 |        $0.025 |
| `GET /v1/proof/:id`          | provenance + historical observation evidence     |        $0.005 |
| `POST /v1/scout`             | richer personalized work shortlist               |         $0.10 |
| `POST /v1/report`            | full market intelligence report                  |   $0.25–$0.50 |

Prices are product hypotheses, not protocol requirements. Test them.

The important thing is the ladder:

```text
frequent machine calls
$0.001–$0.005

analysis calls
$0.01–$0.05

high-value synthesized intelligence
$0.10+
```

Because the judging explicitly includes **actual USDC volume**, an API consisting solely of $0.001 calls would require enormous legitimate traffic to generate meaningful payment volume. The better strategy is a legitimate mixture of high-frequency cheap primitives and more valuable derived intelligence. 

