# 30. Eventually use Algorand State Proofs

Not before registration.

But afterward, this is a killer technical detail.

Algorand State Proofs are network-produced cryptographic commitments to Algorand history and use quantum-safe Falcon signatures. They allow external verifiers to establish Algorand transaction history with reduced trust assumptions. ([Algorand Developer Portal][11])

Eventually:

```text
Moltwork event
→ Merkle proof
→ Oracle snapshot root
→ Algorand transaction
→ Algorand State Proof
```

That's an impressive trust chain:

```text
source observation
↓
Moltwork canonical event
↓
cryptographic dataset commitment
↓
Algorand consensus
↓
State Proof
```

Excellent ETHOnline crossover later too.

