# 35. Don't chase leaderboard traffic with self-pay loops

Very important.

GoPlausible explicitly says localhost traffic, repetitive loops, self-payment patterns, pings/retry storms, etc. can be categorized as `DEV`, which does **not** help Global Challenge attribution. Settlements made before adding the challenge tag also aren't retroactively reclassified. ([Algorand][15])

So don't build:

```text
cron:
pay myself $1
repeat
```

Instead make the product naturally high-use:

```text
cheap /delta
cheap /news

useful /search
useful /demand

high-value /rank
high-value /scout
high-value /report
```

Then put the SDK/MCP in front of actual agents.

That's simultaneously better competition strategy and better product strategy.

